# G3FS Component-20 Q(gamma) Inverse-Source Promotion Contract

G3FS is the strict exit from the finite component-20 theorem to a
characteristic-zero rank theorem.

An accepted packet must derive, from the selected G3FK four-normal source and
with explicit Cox-degree bookkeeping, the mixed-degree inverse primitives

```text
18@15 + 1@16 + 1@19
```

over `Q(gamma)`. It must replay the derivative dimensions

```text
1,3,6,10,15
```

for the degree-19 lane, the three first derivatives of the degree-16 lane and
the direct degree-15 decomposition `18+3+15=36`.

Promotion also requires 100 independent apolar annihilator rows to replay
with literal zero residual in G3EX and one nonzero 36-minor. These give the
rank upper and lower bounds and hence component rank 36 over `Q(gamma)`.

The contract rejects a packet assembled only from finite interpolation,
rational fitting, a post-selected 100-plane or an untyped differential. The
same source formula must produce the primitive lanes. Global H02 closure and
physical promotion are separate downstream gates.

